{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012nAJsqGegDs1Lckmnnheda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No ACL style files available. I'll use a standard article class with reasonable formatting to approximate a conference paper look. Let me write the full paper now.\n\nLet me carefully extract all the numbers I need:\n\n**SciERC NER (8B, N=8, from paper_framing.md)**:\n- greedy F1 = 0.663\n- oracle F1 = 0.776 (headroom 13pp)\n- SJ ρ = 0.360, FK ρ = 0.267, LP ρ = 0.205, EM ρ = 0.295, VC ρ = 0.379\n\n\n- AUROC: EM 0.749, SJ 0.692, VC 0.684, FK 0.629, LP 0.578\n- ECE: EM 0.353, VC 0.381, SJ 0.453, FK 0.451, LP 0.706\n- Selection: LP 0.650, SJ 0.645, ensemble 0.645, greedy 0.644, voting 0.634, random 0.608, oracle 0.776\n- Degeneracy rate = 0.21\n- LP range = 0.041 nats\n\n**SciERC RE (8B, from paper_framing.md)**:\n- greedy F1 = 0.404\n- oracle F1 = 0.585 (headroom 18pp)\n- LP ρ = 0.302 (3-seed mean), SJ ρ = 0.265, FK ρ = 0.254\n- Zero-F1 rate = 43-45%\n- Selection: greedy 0.404 > LP 0.395 > SJ 0.386\n\n**CoNLL NER (8B)**:\n- greedy F1 = 0.912\n- Degeneracy rate = 0.58\n- Oracle headroom = 4.2pp\n- best selection delta = +0.1pp\n\n**Few-NERD (8B, from experiment_data.json)**:\n- greedy F1 = 0.842\n- oracle F1 = 0.908 (headroom 6.6pp)\n- Degeneracy rate = 0.45\n- SJ ρ = 0.41, FK ρ = 0.36\n\nNow I'm looking at the performance metrics across the relation extraction and NER tasks. SciERC shows significant oracle headroom with a high zero-F1 rate, while CoNLL NER is much tighter with minimal selection gains. Few-NERD falls in between with moderate headroom and degeneracy. Looking at the SciERC results, the F1 score is 0.663 with substantial headroom of 13 percentage points and a best delta of +0.6pp, while the R² fit is quite strong at 0.94. The 3-seed experiments show SJ significantly outperforming LP with a p-value of 0.0038, and structural approaches beat surface-level ones at p=0.0005, with confidence intervals narrowing by 30%. The LoRA rank ablation at rank 8 shows greedy achieving 0.648 F1 with low degeneracy.\n\nNow examining the rank 16 results and comparing across model scales—the 8B model shows higher degeneracy than rank 8, and there's a notable 10.6 percentage point gap in degeneracy between the 8B and 4B variants. The scale ablation reveals that the 4B model achieves stronger structural alignment on SciERC NER compared to the 8B, though the 4B selection approach underperforms greedy decoding across all metrics.\n\nLooking at the CoNLL NER results, the 4B model reaches 0.9234 with 1.70 percentage points of headroom. The free-form ablation shows that LP performs similarly whether constrained or unconstrained, with a tied fraction dropping from 59.7% to 57.7% and a parse rate of 99.95%. Within the non-tied subset, LP selection gains 2.9 percentage points over greedy with statistical significance, and the within-instance correlation jumps dramatically from 0.08 to 0.39.\n\nNow I'm ready to write the paper with the title \"Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors: Why Confidence Signals Cannot Scale Structured Information Extraction,\" organizing the results section by section while keeping all the numbers precise.\n\nFor the paper structure, I'm setting up a two-column article format to match conference standards, then mapping out how to integrate all five experiments: the Few-NERD smoke test as a pilot, the full Few-NERD results as the main table, the three-seed SciERC consistency check, the LoRA rank-8 ablation, and the claim audit findings woven throughout. The paper will flow through abstract, introduction, related work, and methodology before diving into the results.\n\nWriting the LaTeX document now... Looking at the ablation studies across different LoRA configurations, free-form variations, and robustness checks across multiple seeds, then wrapping up with discussion and conclusions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":271,"cache_read_input_tokens":43110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":271},"output_tokens":13,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9f5692f-b942-4cae-9f13-3382b875a62b","uuid":"2957a21e-668c-4890-9f3f-7676b554db5d"}
